<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nezahualpilli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1464">1464</a>–<a href="/years/1515">1515</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nezahualpilli was the ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texcoco">Texcoco</a> from 1472 to 1515, son and successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nezahualcoyotl">Nezahualcoyotl</a>. A partner in the Aztec <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Triple Alliance</a>, he was famed as a wise judge, astrologer and poet, and is said to have foretold disasters for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a>. His death led to a disputed succession between his sons that weakened Texcoco on the eve of the Spanish conquest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nezahualpilli.jpg" alt="Nezahualpilli" width="320" height="456" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nezahualpiltzintli.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
